      "gap": "The construction or argument is not written in full: annex:p15.conditional-existence (handbook/annex/p15/conditional-expectation.tex 23-39) applies Radon-Nikodym on (Omega,G,P|_G), obtaining nu_pm(A)=int_A Z_pm d(P|_G), and then asserts that Z_pm have P-integrals EX^pm and that int_A Z dP = nu_+(A)-nu_-(A). The identity int_A W d(P|_G) = int_A W dP for G-measurable W (nonnegative or integrable) is neither proved nor cited, and no handbook result on the route states it. The handbook must supply that step (e.g. G-simple approximation plus monotone convergence on both spaces, or the law-integral theorem for the identity map (Omega,F0)->(Omega,G)) so that the constructed Z is shown to be P-integrable and to satisfy the P-integral identity of def:p15-general-conditional-expectation. Integrability with E|Z|<=E|X| (annex 5-14), a.e. uniqueness (15-21), the X+/X- construction, no completion (41) and the worked boundary (body 365-371, annex 727-739) are present.",
